From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: FullPanel, full screen over the strip beside the notch (experimental)

What: with OMACVM_FULLPANEL=1 (OmacVM.app sets it for one start, for a VM
whose notch setting is FullPanel), a full-screen window on a display with a
camera housing covers the whole display, the strip beside the notch
included, and stays a real macOS full-screen window in a Space of its own.
AppKit itself lays the window out over the whole display: its full-screen
content controller asks whether the window keeps the menu bar's band free
(-[_NSFullScreenContentController reservesSpaceForMenuBarInFullScreen]),
and for a VM window (QemuWindow, OmacVMHeadWindow) in such a full screen
the answer is no. Every other window, and every call off the main thread,
gets AppKit's own answer. No window class or frame setter is overridden
and no full-screen size forced; QEMU's own full-screen resize leaves a
FullPanel window as AppKit laid it out (a guest mode that does not fill
it, the firmware's 1920x1080, is scaled onto it, not the window fitted to
it, which moved it off the strip). The full screen counts once the
window covers the display; a window that does not at didEnterFullScreen
(Split View) keeps AppKit's layout for that full screen. The full-screen
Space's menu bar backdrop is made transparent (SkyLight, that Space only).
With "Keep the Dock away" (QEMU's immersive=on, the app's default) the
menu bar never comes down, as in normal full screen with that setting.
Without it, it comes down from the display's top row as usual: the reveal
is seen through AppKit's full-screen titlebar window (its alpha, observed
with KVO), and while no reveal is on screen that window lets clicks in the
strip through to the VM. After Mission Control, a Space switch, the Dock
or Command-Tab, the backdrop and the options are applied again once
WindowServer has the window back in place (at most 2 s; never a frame).
SLSTransactionCommit returns nothing (macOS 27: w0 is left over), so it is
not read as a status. The guest's size, the full-screen area and the
display arrangement sent to the guest then start at the display's top
edge, and the guest is the whole panel: no rows cut for Omarchy's scale
presets (omacvm-cocoa-clean-size.patch does that below a notch; over the
strip the cut rows were a black band at the bottom, 2940x1900 on a
2940x1912 MacBook Air). Rules in ui/omacvm-fullpanel.h
(omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel-logic.patch). qemu.log: "omacvm: full panel:
strip covered: ..." per full screen that has it (omacvm check reads it),
"strip lost" when AppKit moved the window off the whole display after all
(not for a new display mode: CoreGraphics has it before NSScreen does),
"... normal full screen" when a full screen falls back.

Why: OmacVM.app's own full screen can draw beside the camera itself, so on
that route the guest's bar can sit in the strip without Omanotch's stream
(Omanotch stays the default and the only way on UTM, VMware Fusion and
Parallels, which keep their windows below the notch). Issue #339. This
version replaces the previous FullPanel code (a hook on AppKit's private
full-screen frame, guards on five frame setters, a forced full-screen
content size and hooks on AppKit's menu bar companion's reveal setters),
whose reveal observer, menu bar and presentation logic and frame hook an
audit (2026-10-18) found to be adapted from UTM's camera-housing full
screen (Apache-2.0, which the FSF holds incompatible with GPL-2.0-only
code, and QEMU's binary has such files); this version removes the code
identified as adapted (docs/adr/0044-fullpanel.md, "Replacement").

Fallbacks: without OMACVM_FULLPANEL=1 nothing of it runs. External
displays (no camera housing), macOS's "Always show the menu bar in full
screen" without Keep the Dock away, a reservation method that is missing,
changed, inherited or replaced by other code, any SkyLight function that is
missing, no menu bar transaction from SkyLight, and presentation options
AppKit refuses give normal full screen (logged). A full screen that loses
the strip is not forced back; a full-screen Space moved to a display
without a housing is normal full screen there until it is back.

Credit: Brian Merchant's FullPanel branch for OmacVM (#339). Answering
AppKit's full-screen menu bar reservation question to get the layout was
inspired by Try Omarchy's pull request #361 (themartiano, MIT; no code
from it).
UTM's camera-housing full screen (Turing Software, LLC; UTM PR #7885 and
#7910, Apache-2.0) is prior art for this feature. OmacVM's earlier
version contained code adapted from it; the code identified as adapted is
not in this patch. This is a redesign by authors who had read the earlier
code, not a clean-room implementation.

Upstream: not applicable (private AppKit/SkyLight interfaces, OmacVM's notch).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-fullpanel.sh (the rules, every
notched MacBook's size, external displays, moves between them; with the
patched ui/cocoa.m also the wiring, and that none of the earlier version's
hooks is left); the runtime build compiles it; the strip itself only on a
notched Mac (docs/features.md, FullPanel).

